From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: msi: an environment value that refers to another variable is written REG_EXPAND_SZ

WriteEnvironmentStrings wrote every new value as REG_SZ. Windows Installer
writes one that refers to other variables expandable. Go's installer sets
GOPATH=%USERPROFILE%\go and adds %USERPROFILE%\go\bin to the user's PATH;
as REG_SZ nothing expanded them, every program saw the literal text, and
`go` refused to run at all ("GOPATH entry is relative; must be absolute
path"). A value containing '%' is now written REG_EXPAND_SZ; others keep
their type.

Gate: test/devtools-gate.sh (msienv).
---
--- a/dlls/msi/action.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/action.c
@@ -7009,6 +7009,9 @@
             action |= 0x40000000;
         }
     }
+    /* as Windows Installer does: a value that refers to other variables
+     * (%USERPROFILE%\go) is written expandable, or nothing expands it */
+    if (wcschr( newval, '%' )) type = REG_EXPAND_SZ;
     TRACE("setting %s to %s\n", debugstr_w(name), debugstr_w(newval));
     res = RegSetValueExW( env, name, 0, type, (BYTE *)newval, size );
     if (res)
